---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeadForm from '../../components/LeadForm.astro';
import { STICKY_ABU_DHABI_OFFPLAN } from '../../data/sticky-cta';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Abu Dhabi Off-Plan Investment: Aldar & DMT-Registered Projects"
  description="Abu Dhabi off-plan shortlist with DMT registration checks, Aldar and third-party developers, payment plans, and yield vs appreciation framing."
  stickyCta={STICKY_ABU_DHABI_OFFPLAN}
>
  <section class="site-container py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <span class="badge-pill mb-4">Abu Dhabi off-plan</span>
      <h1 class="mb-4">Abu Dhabi off-plan investment</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
        Saadiyat and Yas launches dominate foreign demand. We prioritise ADX-listed developers and transparent escrow registration.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose mb-10">
      <p><a href="/guides/abu-dhabi-off-plan-guide/">Abu Dhabi off-plan guide</a> · <a href="/developers/aldar/">Aldar review</a></p>

      <h2>How Abu Dhabi off-plan differs from Dubai</h2>
      <p>
        The mechanics rhyme but the paperwork does not. Registration runs through the Department of Municipalities and Transport rather than DLD, transfer is charged at 2% against Dubai's 4%, and escrow obligations sit under Abu Dhabi's own regulations. Eligibility attaches to the specific Investment Zone under Law 13/2019, so confirm the plot status before the developer's marketing language does it for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Aldar dominates delivery volume, which cuts both ways: a strong on-time record and a single counterparty carrying much of the market's completion risk. Verify the record on the specific phase rather than on the corporate average.
      </p>

      <h2>What to check before reserving</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Investment Zone status confirmed on the DMT record for that plot.</li>
        <li>Escrow account named in the SPA verified against the regulator's record.</li>
        <li>Share of the payment plan falling due at handover, and the financing plan for it.</li>
        <li>Service-charge estimate tested against audited budgets in comparable completed stock.</li>
        <li>Tawtheeq-registered rents from handed-over units nearby, not portal asking rents.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Timing the entry</h2>
      <p>
        Off-plan pricing is a trade of time for discount. On an Abu Dhabi island project completing three years out, the buyer forgoes three years of rent while capital stays committed, and the discount has to be worth more than that forgone income plus the risk of a slip. Where it is not, ready stock in the same district is usually the better instrument. Detail in the <a href="/guides/abu-dhabi-off-plan-guide/">Abu Dhabi off-plan guide</a>.
      </p>

    </div>
    <LeadForm title="Abu Dhabi off-plan shortlist" subtitle="Payment plan · handover · visa fit" context="Invest Abu Dhabi off-plan landing" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
